  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry weather continues into the last week of \nOctober.\n\nA dry cold front will push south of the Mason-Dixon Line early\ntoday. In the wake of the cfront, a brief, several-hour uptick \nin north to northeasterly wind will occur across the Susq \nValley and points east during the mid to late morning hours\ntoday. \n\nPWAT values will once again decrease to 0.25 of an inch or less\nfor the midday and afternoon hours today as sfc high pressure \nbuilds into the region with a pronounced upper level ridge \ndeveloping over the eastern US. This will keep dry conditions \naround through at least the beginning of next week with \nseasonably warm days and chilly nights. \n\nHREF probs of temperatures falling below freezing late tonight\nand early Sat are 50 percent or less for Lancaster and Lebanon \nCounties (the only zones where the growing season remains \nactive). \n\nNAM and GFS MOS guidance have shown a slight increase to 33-36F\nin both of those counties. This trend (albeit with still very \nfavorable set up for efficient radiational cooling), has led us \nto hold onto (for another model cycle) the Freeze Watch for \ntonight/Saturday morning.\n\nWidespread frost appears likely acrs much of these 2 counties\n(and elsewhere across the rest of the CWA), but there is still\nsome question if we'll see many sub-freezing min temps in the\ncurrent Watch area.",
